---
description: API layering, routers, services, repositories
globs: apps/api/app/routers/**, apps/api/app/services/**, apps/api/app/repositories/**, apps/api/app/core/**, apps/api/app/domain/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Routers: receive request, check role, call one service, return. No SQL, no business logic.
- Services: business logic. Call repositories and ports.
- Repositories: the only place with SQL. Parameterised queries only.
- Domain: pure code, no I/O. Metric definitions live here, once.
- org_id comes from the authenticated principal only
- Missing record and another org's record return the identical 404
- (client) routes return verified data only
